pi-standalone

Independent fork of Pi v1.3.0 by Mario Zechner and contributors.
Upstream: https://github.com/earendil-works/pi
Baseline commit: 71023aec1546d6d677a65669c5665c0927ce0dd0
The upstream MIT copyright and permission notice are retained in LICENSE.

Changes for pi-standalone include single-file Node packaging, embedded resources
and workers, in-memory Photon/Babel decompression, a private Jiti extension
module graph, a TypeBox constructor guard adjustment for minified classes,
Rust/WASM search integration, and native-platform adapters. Dependency JavaScript
is bundled and minified while function and class names are preserved.

Third-party software retains its original licenses and attribution notices.
The generated search WASM includes its Rust dependency/toolchain notices in
packages/tui/src/standalone-search-wasm-data.ts. Additional prebuilt-component
notices and reviewed package-license supplements are in
scripts/standalone-notices/. The builder includes these and installed package
notices in the single JavaScript artifact; these notices are not replaced by
this project's MIT license.

The independent DOOM overlay demonstration includes a separately packaged
GPLv3-or-later engine (its input files retain their GPLv2-or-later and
GPLv3-or-later notices). Pi's core and packaging code retain their own licenses.
Complete corresponding source for the rebuilt DOOM component is provided in
scripts/standalone-notices/doom-corresponding-source.tar.gz and as the same-named
asset beside pi-standalone.mjs at:
https://github.com/seo-rii/pi-standalone/releases/tag/standalone-v1.3.0-preview.1
The archive also identifies the public historical sources and original build
files associated with the inherited upstream example binaries. A third party
redistributing those binaries must preserve the applicable license notices and
provide the corresponding source under the component's license terms.

The published upstream records do not reconstruct a complete build inventory
for every prebuilt component. See PUBLICATION.md and the notice manifests for
the exact available evidence and the remaining provenance limitations.
